From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:36:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: qcom-ipq9574: handle 2500BASE-X out-of-band status

The TP-LINK TL-SM410U has no PHY accessible over I2C and its SFP quirk
disables in-band autonegotiation. In that mode phylink passes
PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_DISABLED, while the SFP state machine already
gates the link using its LOS-driven link-up and link-down callbacks.

Do not require the PCS in-band link bit in this mode. It remains clear
on IPQ5332 even when the module state is link_up, leaving the netdevice
without carrier. Report the fixed 2500BASE-X state and retain the PCS
status read for modes which do provide in-band status.

The source hunks were generated with diff -u from the prepared kernel
source before this patch.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
 drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-qcom-ipq9574.c
@@ -217,11 +217,24 @@ static void ipq_pcs_get_state_sgmii(stru
 }
 
 static void ipq_pcs_get_state_2500basex(struct ipq_pcs *qpcs,
+					unsigned int neg_mode,
 					struct phylink_link_state *state)
 {
 	unsigned int val;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* A copper SFP without PHY I2C access cannot provide 2500BASE-X
+	 * in-band status. In that mode the SFP state machine already gates
+	 * phylink through its LOS-driven link_up and link_down callbacks.
+	 */
+	if (neg_mode == PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_DISABLED) {
+		state->link = true;
+		state->speed = SPEED_2500;
+		state->duplex = DUPLEX_FULL;
+		state->pause |= MLO_PAUSE_TXRX_MASK;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	ret = regmap_read(qpcs->regmap, PCS_MII_STS(0), &val);
 	if (ret) {
 		state->link = 0;
@@ -825,7 +838,7 @@ static void ipq_pcs_get_state(struct phy
 		ipq_pcs_get_state_sgmii(qpcs, index, state);
 		break;
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX:
-		ipq_pcs_get_state_2500basex(qpcs, state);
+		ipq_pcs_get_state_2500basex(qpcs, neg_mode, state);
 		break;
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_USXGMII:
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_10G_QXGMII:
